# Public frontend configuration only.
# Never put database, session, HMAC, or service-role secrets here.

# Leave this unset for local dev. The CRA dev server proxies /api calls to the backend via
# src/setupProxy.js — this works both at plain localhost and when the frontend is accessed
# through a tunnel (ngrok, etc.) from another device, including full-page navigations to a
# server-rendered endpoint (e.g. the Admin QR print sheet), not just fetch()/XHR calls. A
# hardcoded absolute URL like http://localhost:4000/api only works when the browser itself is
# on this machine; from any other origin it fails with a CORS error and/or the browser's
# "local network access" permission prompt, since the browser would be trying to reach a
# private-network address from a public origin.
#
# Only set this when the frontend and backend are deployed to genuinely
# separate domains (e.g. Vercel frontend + Render backend):
# REACT_APP_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com/api

# Not needed. This project intentionally uses src/setupProxy.js instead of package.json's
# simple "proxy" field (the latter silently breaks full-page navigation to a server-rendered
# /api endpoint), and webpack-dev-server's Host-header check is keyed off that "proxy" field
# specifically — so it stays disabled by default here without needing this override, including
# for tunnel access. Kept documented in case a future change reintroduces the "proxy" field.
# DANGEROUSLY_DISABLE_HOST_CHECK=true
